!PlexRO - a Plex client for RISC OS                  0.1.0-test1
===================================================================

PlexRO browses the films and TV programmes on a Plex Media Server and
plays them in ReelEGL or Reel, the video players from riscos-ffmpeg.
Files the players can play as they are go to the player directly.
Everything else is converted by the server, as it plays, into a stream
the players can handle: H.264 video with stereo AAC sound.

This is a test build: it hasn't been tried on RISC OS yet.

PlexRO is a working name. Plex is a trademark of Plex, Inc.; PlexRO isn't
made by Plex or connected with it.

Starting
--------
Double-click !PlexRO: its icon (a screen with posters and a play button)
appears on the icon bar. The first time, click Select on it to sign in.

Signing in
----------
The sign-in window shows a four-letter code. On any computer or phone, go
to plex.tv/link, sign in to your Plex account there, and type the code.
PlexRO checks every 2 seconds, and carries on by itself once the code has
been typed: it finds your servers and opens the browser. PlexRO never sees
your password. A code runs out after a while: New code gets another.

A server on your own network can be used without plex.tv: type its
address (such as 192.168.1.10; :32400 is added) and a token (the server's
or your account's X-Plex-Token), then click Use these.

The browser
-----------
Select on the icon bar icon opens it. At the top: Back, where you are,
and a status line. Below them, a poster for each film, show, season or
episode, with its name and (for example) its year, "S1 E3" or
"3 seasons". An orange corner marks what you haven't watched; an orange
bar under a poster shows how far you got.

  double-click   open a library, show or season; play a video
  Return         the same, for the poster that's selected
  arrow keys     move the selection
  Backspace, Escape  go back

The top list is Continue watching, then your libraries. Films and TV
libraries open; music and photo libraries aren't handled yet.

Menu on a poster:
  Play (Open)         as a double-click
  Resume from h:mm:ss where Plex says you stopped. The server streams it
                      from there (copying the video when it can)
  Play from start     from the beginning
  Save original file > the file itself, onto your disc (below)
  Mark watched, Mark unwatched
  Back, Refresh

Playing
-------
PlexRO gives the video to the player chosen on Player on the icon's menu:
ReelEGL (the default) or Reel. If it's running, it gets the video at
once; if not, PlexRO starts it. The Filer must have seen the player's
application (open the directory it's in, or add it to your boot
sequence), or PlexRO can't find it.

The status line says how it will play:
  "Direct play: ..."         the file itself: nothing is converted
  "Converted by the server"  the server converts it, and says why (for
                             example HEVC video, 10-bit video, or a bit
                             rate above the quality's limit)

Quality on the icon's menu sets the limits, for direct play and for
what the server converts to: 1080p (10 Mbit/s), 720p (4 Mbit/s, the
default) or 480p (2 Mbit/s). The Raspberry Pi 4 decodes H.264 on one
core, so the bit rate matters as much as the size. Untick Direct play
when possible to have the server convert everything.

Saving the original file
------------------------
Move to the right of Save original file on a poster's menu: a save box
opens. Drag its icon to a directory display (or type a full path and
click Save). The file is saved a piece at a time, so the desktop carries
on; the status line shows how far it's got. Stop saving is on the same
menu while it's saving.

RISC OS's filing systems hold files of up to 4GB, so bigger files are
refused at once.

Choices
-------
Kept in Choices:PlexRO.Choices: the player, the quality, direct play,
the server in use, and the tokens that sign PlexRO in to plex.tv and the
server. Anyone who can read your Choices can use those tokens: Sign out
on the icon's menu removes them.

Needs
-----
- RISC OS 5 on an ARMv7 machine (Raspberry Pi 2/3/4/400 and so on).
- ReelEGL or Reel 0.1.17 or later (riscos-ffmpeg), which plays what
  PlexRO finds. Their sound needs SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager:
  download ssb.zip from https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html
  and merge its !System. John Duffell's own site (now on the Internet
  Archive) has more details:
  https://web.archive.org/web/20110920080106/http://www.duffell.riscos.me.uk/
- SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later and ARMEABISupport (PackMan).
- AcornSSL (RISC OS 5.28 or later) for signing in with a code, and for
  servers reached through their plex.direct addresses.

!Run loads the modules it needs. PThreadTicker (UnixLib's thread timer)
is in the application directory.

Debugging: *Set PlexRO$Debug 1 before starting it lets FFmpeg's network
messages through (to see them, run !RunImage from a TaskWindow).

